--TEST--
an unqualified shape written at a Core\Request decode site names the field and the shape, and the three members that take one agree rather than each answering for itself — `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`, `rule:security/tainted-sources`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:security/tainted-sources` makes the body and the query alike a peer's octets, so a
// shape written at one of these three doors is the declaration those octets
// land in. An unqualified text field is a promise nothing is making, and it is
// refused where the shape is written: there is no declaration further down the
// file to carry the qualifier instead, which is what separates a shape from
// `rule:core-classes/derive-attribute`'s deriving class, whose property is reported at its
// declaration by the same code.
var $body = Core\Request::jsonAs<{name: string}>();
var $query = Core\Request::queryAs<{q: string}>();
var $form = Core\Request::postAs<{email: string}>();

// A field carrying no text is not in the diagnosis at all -- an `int` holds no
// octets a sink could read, so a shape of them needs no qualifier and this
// line is silent.
var $page = Core\Request::queryAs<{page: int}>();

// `tainted {…}` is the answer to the verbosity rather than an opt-out, and it
// distributes to every text-carrying field, so one word answers a shape of two
// and this line is silent as well.
var $ok = Core\Request::postAs<tainted {email: string, note: string}>();
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0810]: `name` is declared `string` in `{name: string}`, and `Core\Request::jsonAs` answers a peer's octets
  --> case.nvs:9:34
%A
error[E0810]: `q` is declared `string` in `{q: string}`, and `Core\Request::queryAs` answers a peer's octets
   --> case.nvs:10:36
%A
error[E0810]: `email` is declared `string` in `{email: string}`, and `Core\Request::postAs` answers a peer's octets
   --> case.nvs:11:34
